P5-bin-001, blocked by write scope only (aegis-iso belongs to the iso units): the worker-side negative control
`dumpable-1` of oracles/p2-e2e ("PR_SET_DUMPABLE(0) skipped: /proc/<pid> entries owned by the user", expected red
family `dumpable.`). No crate has it, so without this patch the real self-test cannot catch that mutant. It compiles
only with aegis-iso feature `mutants` (enabled by aegis-p2 `mutants` / aegis-bin `p2-mutants`, built only into
target/p2-mutants*, PLAN-5 D15) and is selected at run time by AEGIS_P2_MUTANT=dumpable-1; golden builds are
unchanged (`mutant_dumpable_1()` is the constant false). Applied for the P5-bin-001 self-test run, which caught the
mutant on 7 checks (dumpable.cordons, dumpable.forkwasm-child, dumpable.forkwasm-workers, ...).
Apply from the repo root: git apply crates/aegis-bin/tests/p2-patches/aegis-iso-dumpable-1-mutant.patch

